      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Video 1> is the source for the target video edit: a single illustration or manga panel placed on a plain canvas with blank margins, held as a still for the whole clip, showing one character in a specific pose, camera angle, and framing. Its composition is kept exactly: the body pose, limb and hand positions, head direction, camera angle, and the character's placement and size inside the canvas. Its original character's face, hair, and clothing are not kept, and any monochrome manga rendering, screentone, panel border, speech balloons, and text are not kept.\n<Subject 1> is the character that replaces the character in <Video 1>, taken from <Picture 1>: a young woman with very long straight black hair in a high ponytail with blunt bangs and a thin black halo ring floating above her head, red eyes and a calm expression, wearing a skintight black-and-white bodysuit with red lines and a red front zipper, black gloves, and black boots, drawn in the clean full-color anime style of <Picture 1>. Only the design is taken from <Picture 1>; its pose, framing, and background are not used.\n\nsummary:\n[video editing] The target video is an edited version of <Video 1>. The character in <Video 1> is replaced by <Subject 1>: her hair becomes very long straight black hair in a high ponytail with blunt bangs and a thin black halo ring floating above her head, her eyes become red eyes and a calm expression, and her clothing is replaced by a skintight black-and-white bodysuit with red lines and a red front zipper, black gloves, and black boots as in <Picture 1>, keeping the exact pose, limb and hand positions, head direction, camera angle, framing, placement, and size of the original character on every frame. The blank margins of the canvas are filled with the same plain background so the whole frame reads as one complete image. The result is rendered in full color in the anime style of <Picture 1>, with a plain simple background and without screentone, panel borders, speech balloons, or text. The camera is locked and nothing moves.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Video 1> (whole video): partially_preserved - the composition is kept frame for frame; the original character's face, hair, and clothing are discarded and replaced, and any monochrome rendering, screentone, panel border, balloons, and text are discarded.\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the hair, eyes, clothing, colors, and art style of <Picture 1> are used for the character.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target is one still full-color anime illustration held for the whole clip, not a collage, split screen, or sequence.\n[Shot 1] The shot is <Video 1> with a locked camera and the same framing. The character is redrawn as <Subject 1>, occupying exactly the same place and size in the frame and holding exactly the same pose as the original character in <Video 1>: the same body orientation, the same limb and hand positions, and the same head direction. She has very long straight black hair in a high ponytail with blunt bangs and a thin black halo ring floating above her head, red eyes and a calm expression, and wears a skintight black-and-white bodysuit with red lines and a red front zipper, black gloves, and black boots, as in <Picture 1>, and none of the original character's hair or clothing remain. She is drawn in the clean full-color anime style of <Picture 1> with clean lines and flat cel shading. The background is plain and simple and extends across the whole canvas, including the former margins. There is no screentone, no panel border, no speech balloon, and no text. Nothing moves from the first frame to the last.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nN/A\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "value": "Bold comic-book ink style, heavy linework, red and blue-black palette, night city. Use <Picture 2> and <Picture 1> as reference frames and <Audio 1> exactly as it is.\nCUT 1: top-down view of the little boy superhero on the rooftop — red cape fluttering in the wind, hands planted on his hips, freckles and a cocky grin as he looks straight up into the camera. The camera slowly descends toward him as he delivers his line — as he speaks, comic-book graphic overlay text word by word in sync with his voice: \"GET READY TO\" - \"MEET\" — \"YOUR\" — \"MAKER\" — huge jagged comic lettering, white with heavy black outlines and red drop shadows, tilted at scrappy angles, until the three words hang stacked in the air above him between his face and the lens.\nTRANSITION: a violent WHIP PAN off the rooftop that SMEARS the floating words away with it, motion-streaked —\nCUT 2: low hero angle on the colossal black mech-kaiju towering over the skyline as it rears back and unleashes a GIANT terrifying ROAR — jaws wide with fangs, red eyes and chest-core flaring blinding bright, blue lightning arcing off its head, the roar's shockwave rippling dust and rattling windows down the buildings, comic-style speed-lines and ink splatter bursting from the impact of the sound. It leans INTO the camera as the roar peaks. Hold on the roar."
      },
      "color": "#322",
      "bgcolor": "#533"
    },
